updated: 2026-11-14
changelog: |
  0.2.0 — the caller pins the hub's floating major tag: fleet-conformance.yml@v2
  with `hub-ref: v2`, so the checker runs at the same version as the
  workflow (docs/WORKFLOW-VERSIONING.md). 0.1.0 called @main, which fails
  UPS-QA-40 and UPS-WORK-10 in every repo that took it (24 callers on
  2026-11-14). The caller now carries a `# kit: conformance vX.Y.Z` stamp.
  archive/conformance-0.1.0.yml keeps the old shape, so --upgrade
  recognises the byte-identical machine seeds and repins them.
  0.1.0 — initial thin caller of the reusable fleet-conformance.yml workflow.
  Advisory by default (gate: false); a repo flips it once its MUST rows pass.
notes: |
  - Snapshot to archive/ before editing this template so --upgrade can still
    recognise machine-seeded copies (same rule as the other kits).
